+> **Created:** 2026-09-13 16:2xZ | **Author:** FX-EXEC2 (STA-03, AUDIT_EXEC 842bbffa) | **Status:** documentation only, no behaviour change | **Void when:** `book_source` in config/book.json is not `external`, or scheduler/anchor_loop.py changes the branches cited below
+
+# State files with no reader while `book_source = external`
+
+The executor has run the external combo book since 2026-08-22 08Z (`config/book.json` `"book_source": "external"`). Two
+state files belong to the retired internal composer. In external mode they are never written, and nothing reads them.
+They are listed here so that a reader of `state/` does not treat them as live inputs.
+
+| File | Written by | Read by | Last write | Why it exists |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `state/live/no_trade_band.json` | `scheduler/anchor_loop.py` L1891-1901, inside the internal-book `else` branch of the no-trade band (`LG.apply_no_trade_band`) | **nothing**: grep over `live/ scheduler/ ops/ signal/`, `~/guard_twin`, `~/regime_dash` finds no reader | `A1787371250` = 2026-08-22 04:00:50Z, the last internal-book anchor | receipt of the neutral no-trade band `b=0.002` (PROPOSAL_neutral_band 8e499dac); in external mode the band is skipped: `_nb = {"applied": False, "skipped": "external_book", ...}` (L1874-1880) |
+| `<mode root>/harvest_ema.json` (`state/live/harvest_ema.json` in LIVE) | `scheduler/anchor_loop.py` L1695-1755, inside the internal composer (`LG.apply_harvest_ema`) | the same internal branch, on the next internal anchor only | absent under `state/live` (removed by `ops/resume_from_trip.sh` L102/L302 on every resume); the DRY_RUN tree's copy is from 2026-08-22 | per-name EMA memory of the harvest-speed transform (PREREG_harvest_speed_acceptance 53ab6f5a) |
+
+## What would make them live again
+
+Both files matter only if `book_source` returns to `internal`. The config itself says that needs a user ruling and a
+check of the internal data/model chain first (`config/book.json` `external_book._rollback`).
+
+**Before any such switch, the harvest EMA memory must be cleared.** The EMA would otherwise carry weights from
+2026-08-22 across the gap (see tests_harvest_ema [W]: reset-on-flatten and the resume-script removal).
+
+## Retirement (operator step, not done here)
+
+At the next state clean-up, rename `state/live/no_trade_band.json` to
+`state/live/no_trade_band.json.retired_<utc>`. No code reads it, so renaming changes no behaviour.
+
+`harvest_ema.json` is already absent under `state/live`.
+
+Nothing in this repository was changed to retire them. STA-03 is documentation.
